            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "What could push airlines to tipping point if US shutdown drags on",
            "description": "<p>Delta Air Lines (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DAL\">DAL</a>) stock is lifting off on Thursday<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/delta-reports-strong-q3-earnings-ceo-sees-significant-improvement-in-revenue-outlook-103521470.html\"> after topping third quarter estimates:</a> revenue of $15.2 billion (vs. estimates of $15.1 billion) and adjusted earnings of $1.71 per share (vs. estimates of $1.56). As the US government's shutdown moves into its ninth day, what sort of disruptions could airline operators see in the coming days if the shutdown drags on longer?</p>\n<p>Hickory Global Partners president and managing partner Chris Dane and Yahoo Finance senior reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/pras-subramanian/\">Pras Subramanian</a> weigh in.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Delta Air Lines (DAL) stock is lifting off on Thursday after topping third quarter estimates: revenue of $15.2 billion (vs. estimates of $15.1 billion) and adjusted earnings of $1.71 per share (vs. estimates of $1.56). As the US government's shutdown moves into its ninth day, what sort of disruptions could airline operators see in the coming days if the shutdown drags on longer? Hickory Global Partners president and managing partner Chris Dane and Yahoo Finance senior reporter Pras Subramanian weigh in. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more&nbsp;Market Catalysts.",
