            "title": "Delta flies high on strong Q4 outlook, lifting American & United",
            "description": "<p>Delta Air Lines (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DAL\">DAL</a>) stock surged after releasing stronger-than-expected earnings and an upbeat outlook for the fourth quarter, driven by premium and business customers.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/pras-subramanian/\">Pras Subramanian</a> outlines the details of the earnings print and examines the rise in other airline stocks, like American Airlines (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAL\">AAL</a>) and United Airlines (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/UAL\">UAL</a>).</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/morning-brief/\">Morning Brief</a>.</p>",
